Usage: basename NAME [SUFFIX]
basename OPTION... NAME...

Print NAME with any leading directory components removed.
If specified, also remove a trailing SUFFIX.

OPTIONS:
  -a, --multiple    support multiple arguments and treat each as a NAME
      --mul         alias for --multiple
  -s, --suffix ARG  remove a trailing SUFFIX; implies -a
      --suf ARG     alias for --suffix
  -z, --zero        end each output line with NUL, not newline
      --ze          alias for --zero
      --help        display this help and exit
  -V, --version     output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
